{"id":716,"date":"2020-11-02T13:56:56","date_gmt":"2020-11-02T21:56:56","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=716"},"modified":"2024-08-30T09:46:44","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T16:46:44","slug":"functions","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/functions\/","title":{"rendered":"3B: Functions"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d75600\" name=\"6a22140d75600\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to pair to Blockly <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/\">here<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d7573c\" name=\"6a22140d7573c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are functions?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Functions are a way to save time and energy by storing commonly used blocks of code in one named set. For a real-world example, when you\u2019re drinking a glass of water, the entire task might look like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Find glass<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bring over to water source<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pour water into glass<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure water doesn\u2019t overflow!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drink water<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">But instead of saying all of that, you could just say you\u2019re drinking water! Functions work the same way. Multiple lines of code can be included in one function that you name and set up to be used in your program.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d7579b\" name=\"6a22140d7579b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Defining a function<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To define a function, or explain what is going to be in it, you will need the to do something block in the pink functions menu. Drag that to your workspace and then name your function in the white box. This should be something memorable that describes your function well. Next, drag the blocks you need into the function. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;717&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try it now! Make a function that has the name \u201cpushup\u201d and that has your CoDrone Mini do a pushup. It should take off, hover, and land. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;720&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;721&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d757ee\" name=\"6a22140d757ee\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Using a function<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once you define a function, you should see a block for it in the functions menu. To use it, drag it into your workspace and drop it to wherever you would like to see it in your program.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Remember your very first challenge with CoDrone Mini? You needed to see how many drone pushups you could do. Try doing this now with a loop and your new function!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;723&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d7583c\" name=\"6a22140d7583c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Functions in flight<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use a function in your flight program, drag its function block to where you would like to see it in your code.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try this out now! After your CoDrone Mini does a few drone pushups, have it take off, pitch forward at 100% power for 1 second, and then land.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;725&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d75881\" name=\"6a22140d75881\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Warning<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you plan on using your function later on, do not remove it from your workspace! Doing this will delete the entire function and you will not be able to locate it in the functions menu.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22140d758ca\" name=\"6a22140d758ca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Initialize<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Write functions so that CoDrone Mini can fly in your name\u2019s initials! Start with the initial for your first name and the initial for your last name, and then use them in a flight program. Have a super long name? Do what you can after your first and last initials!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Getting Started [vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/functions\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1671,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1746,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2125,2131,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-716","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-functions","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-senior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/716","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":8,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/716\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12820,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/716\/revisions\/12820"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1671"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=716"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=716"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=716"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}